# Creative UI & Taste Rules

## 1. Anti-Generic Layout Guardrails
- **NEVER** build standard alternating "Image on Left, Text on Right" sections.
- Use dynamic, asymmetric grids, layered bento box layouts, and intentional editorial whitespace.
- Implement overlapping sections using negative margins, absolute positioning anchors, and high Z-index depth layers.

## 2. Visual Polish & "Taste" Layer
- **Typography Over Everything:** Use high-contrast type scaling (e.g., massive header fonts tracking-tighter paired with ultra-clean micro-copy).
- **Gradients:** Absolutely NO generic diagonal gradients. Use multi-stop mesh gradients, soft glowing radial orbs (`bg-[radial-gradient(...)]`), or strict monochromatic palettes with high-fidelity accent strokes.
- **Glassmorphism & Depth:** Maximize backdrop-blur layers, thin 1px semi-transparent borders (`border-white/10`), and subtle layered box shadows instead of harsh solid cards.

## 3. Motion & Micro-interactions
- Every interactive element (buttons, cards, links) MUST have an elegant transition state.
- Integrate **Framer Motion** or native CSS keyframes for layout-reveal triggers, magnetic hover tracking, and smooth stagger-fade text entrances.
- Keep animations snappy and luxurious (e.g., `transition: all 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`).
